{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "c3a71f9e0c34437aa59c92b8e78cc57d",
    "m_Title": "<-",
    "m_Content": "If you have no need for the palette feature you can just hook this \"Add\" function, the \"Base Color\" of the fragment shader.\n\nThis also adds more colors to the render after quantization. \nYou can remove this and use the divide node below and hook it to the \"Base Color\" If you don't want any extra colors.",
